---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/base-layout.astro'
import { withBase } from '@/lib/site'

const differences = [
  [
    'Release status',
    'Active development, not yet tagged as a modern release.',
    'Supported architecture descended from 0.3.0. Receives compatibility maintenance.',
  ],
  [
    'Specialists',
    'Ordinary Pi sessions in named Herdr tabs or tmux windows. Private messaging stays connected while you type.',
    'Managed Pi RPC subprocesses. Manual takeover disconnects managed private delivery.',
  ],
  [
    'Memory',
    'Shared Markdown in memory/, chat-local notes, and house history through clawa_memory and clawa_history.',
    'Shared SQLite notes through remember, bounded recent-session search through recall, and a vault/ for shaped knowledge.',
  ],
  [
    'Continuity',
    'Pi owns compaction. Optional Pi Codex owns its configured continuity. Explicit /memory remember queues private consolidation.',
    'Pi owns compaction. Clawa can run an in-session memory pass near the context boundary.',
  ],
  [
    'Living documents',
    'Text refreshes in native structured prompt sections before each turn.',
    'A hidden hydration message persists a snapshot at session and compaction boundaries.',
  ],
  [
    'First run',
    'Creates the home, then waits for your first message or task. Global installs stay dormant outside configured homes.',
    'Bootstraps the home and starts the opening conversation automatically.',
  ],
  [
    'Discord',
    'An optional bot connection in each main or specialist Pi tab. Still WIP.',
    'A shared gateway with routed workers. Still WIP.',
  ],
]
---

<BaseLayout title="Modern and legacy" description="Choose the right Clawa branch and understand what changes when moving from 0.3.0." current="versions">
  <main id="main-content" class="site-shell standalone-page comparison-page" tabindex="-1">
    <header class="doc-header">
      <h1>Modern and legacy</h1>
      <p class="lede">Same idea. Different foundations.</p>
    </header>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        Clawa has two branches, not two settings you can toggle. <strong>Modern</strong> is where
        new architecture lands. <strong>Legacy</strong> maintains the architecture descended from 0.3.0.
        Both give a Pi agent a living home, specialist Clawas, and Pulses.
      </p>
      <p>
        The modern branch is unreleased. A package version still reading <code>0.3.0</code> does
        not make a modern checkout the 0.3.0 release. The unchanged <code>v0.3.0</code> tag belongs
        to legacy and does not include later maintenance. Both branches require Pi <code>0.99.2</code>
        or newer. Legacy does not mean an older Pi installation.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="comparison-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Branch comparison">
      <table class="comparison-table">
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">What changes</th><th scope="col">Modern</th><th scope="col">Legacy</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {differences.map(([subject, modern, legacy]) => (
            <tr><th scope="row">{subject}</th><td>{modern}</td><td>{legacy}</td></tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <div class="branch-links">
      <a class="primary-link" href={withBase('/modern/docs/getting-started/installation/')}>Install modern</a>
      <a href={withBase('/legacy/docs/getting-started/installation/')}>Install legacy</a>
    </div>
    <section class="prose migration-summary">
      <h2>Moving an existing home</h2>
      <p>
        This is a migration, not just a branch rename. Stop the old main session and its workers
        before launching modern. Existing <code>vault/</code> files move into <code>memory/</code>;
        SQLite notes are imported without deleting the old database. Conflicts stop the migration
        rather than overwrite files.
      </p>
      <p>
        Herdr or tmux is needed to launch modern specialists. Discord setup also changes:
        stop the old gateway before updating, then reconnect each home's bot through
        <code>/discord</code>. Tokens and routes are not migrated automatically.
      </p>
      <p>
        Read <a href={withBase('/modern/docs/operate/upgrading/')}>the upgrade guide</a>
        before changing a live home. Switching back to legacy code does not undo a home migration.
      </p>
      <h2>Which docs am I reading?</h2>
      <p>
        Every guide has a Modern or Legacy selector. It takes you to the same topic in the other
        edition when that topic exists. Legacy pages come from one commit of the maintained legacy
        branch, not a fixed copy of the old tag. Any historical references to <code>master</code>
        describe the former branch name. Use modern's
        <a href={withBase('/modern/docs/project/release-policy/')}>release policy</a>
        for the current branch and publishing process.
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
